				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12507613/humanism-and-aesthetics#post-4356001</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Sep 2019 19:42:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Pedantique</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3118444</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It does indeed introduce this GOI, but that feels like about all that happens here. I'm all for introductory pieces if they're clearly building up to something interesting, but this feels more like a lot of setup for one guy's Bond villain speech and some worldbuilding exposition. The translation's solid, and everything reads well, but I'm just not feeling it as something that stands on its own.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12507613#post-4355951</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12507613/humanism-and-aesthetics#post-4355951</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Sep 2019 18:01:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Uncle Nicolini</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3487700</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hello friends.</p> <p>This tale is, as you may have guessed, from the French branch and introduces one of their favorite GoIs, the Humanist Gentlemen. They are a very interesting group that share ties with SAPPHIRE, but are more akin to the Serpent's Hand. I recommend you check out their <a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/les-gentilshommes-humanistes-centre">hub</a> over on the INT wiki to learn more if you liked what you read.</p> <p>Until next week!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
